# #5841: the split's half of the Dekker pair must persist the narrow before it reads the row.
MODULE: HandOffBoundSplitReadsRowBeforePersist
TARGET: HandOffBound
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the split reads the epoch row before persisting its narrowed state, so both reads can miss the other's write
PERTURBS: SplitPersist, SplitRowRead
BOUNDS: WithStaleDonor = TRUE, WithPreArm = TRUE, MaxWindows = 1

--- FIND
    /\ hoOpen
    /\ sNarrowed
    /\ bst = "idle"
--- REPLACE
    /\ hoOpen
\* MUTATION: the row is read before the narrow is persisted.
    /\ bst = "idle"
--- END

--- FIND
    /\ hoOpen
    /\ ~sNarrowed
    /\ sNarrowed' = TRUE
--- REPLACE
    /\ hoOpen
    /\ ~sNarrowed
\* MUTATION: the narrow is persisted after the row is read and bumped.
    /\ bst = "done"
    /\ sNarrowed' = TRUE
--- END
